## Taskbar Module - Commercial License Required

The following components are excluded from the open source license above and
are subject to a separate commercial license:

- The files `src/taskbar-pin.c` and `src/taskbar.c` and all their functions
- Code directly responsible for writing to the Windows Taskband registry,
  constructing, repairing or updating PIDL blob entries, injecting BEEF001D
  extension blocks, or acquiring the `TaskbarPinListMutex` system mutex
- Code directly responsible for setting window AppUserModel properties to
  control taskbar buttons, refreshing taskbar icons through shell change
  notifications, or detecting snap groups
- Anything for the purpose of programmatic taskbar pinning or of controlling
  the taskbar's buttons, pins and icons

Collectively referred to as the "Taskbar Module."

The notification-area code (`src/tray.c`) is not part of the Taskbar Module:
it is under the open source license above.

